# LoRaSS

LoRaSS is a custom communication device built around LoRa technology, allowing two (or more) devices to exchange short messages over radio. It features five buttons: four for entering messages using a custom input system and one dedicated button to save or send the composed message, allowing an entire message to be transmitted in a single operation. The device also includes a display to preview outgoing messages and read received ones, as well as an LED and a buzzer to provide visual and audio feedback when messages are received (like a morse code machine)

## Features

- **LoRa Communication:** Exchange messages wirelessly using LoRa radio technology.
- **Message Input:** Four buttons are used to enter the desired characters.
- **OLED Display:** Preview messages before sending and read incoming messages.
- **Misc:** A LED and a buzzer indicate when a message is received.

## Hardware Design

The device is powered by a Raspberry Pi Pico ( as mentioned in the other repos, its my fav board) and uses a LoRa radio module for wireless communication. The PCB integrates the display, buttons, buzzer, LED and antenna circuitry.


